WEBVTT

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.900
<i>GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:25.280
I shall show you
the Japanese <i>yokai</i> killing each other.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:29.030
If we drive out Agnes,
they probably won't attack us anymore.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.290
<i>The world you see isn't all there is.</i>

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.090
<i>There are things you can't see.</i>

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:44.970
<i>See? In the darkness behind you...</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>Slumbering in bed in the morning</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>asa wa nedoko de gu gu gu</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>Ghosts don't have school</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>obakenya gakkou mo</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>Or tests or anything</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>shiken mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>minna de utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>Sports festivals in the graveyard at night</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>yoru wa hakaba de undoukai</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>Ghosts don't die</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>obake wa shinanai</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>Or get sick or anything</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>byouki mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:55.560
CHAPTER 34

00:02:56.010 --> 00:03:00.390
EMPEROR BACKBEARD

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:04.020
"Yokai Bus to
the Annual Winter Getaway"...

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.610
I guess it's already that season again.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:11.150
Food from the sea, food from
the mountains, rustic hot springs...

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.570
Massages and body scrubs...

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:15.370
Hup!

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:18.250
And all night mah-jong!

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:21.580
Hooray for being born a Japanese <i>yokai</i>!

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:23.630
Hey, Rat Man!

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:27.750
Wh-What?

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:31.130
You remember last year, don't you?!

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:40.810
You smell something?

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.190
It's a sulfur spring after all.

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:44.440
Wait!

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:57.200
Whoops, here comes another one.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:06.460
I wonder why
farts in the bath are so smelly.

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:08.130
Don't come!

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.130
You're banned!

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:14.090
I'm looking forward to it.

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:20.350
Bowl baths are good, but a hot spring
once in a while hits the spot.

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:23.190
What's wrong, Kitaro?

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:29.480
Actually, Agnes hasn't responded to
the invite I sent.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:35.320
"Invitation to the GeGeGe Forest
Annual Winter Getaway"...

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:37.120
That sounds like fun!

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:41.620
Have you ever tried a Japanese hot spring?
They feel really good!

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:42.580
Wait...

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:44.870
Shouldn't you reply to this?

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.880
It seems like a trip just for friends.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:54.720
Besides, they probably just invited me
as a formality.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:59.720
And we're only working together
temporarily while searching for the ring.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:03.430
And I'm a Western <i>yokai</i>.

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:07.650
What do <i>you</i> want to do?

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:12.190
Do you want to go? Or don't you?

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:36.130
It's getting chilly.

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:11.590
Kitaro.

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:15.510
Sorry, sorry. We're late.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:21.760
Is this all that's going?

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:24.220
And the bus isn't here yet.

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:26.180
The getaway's cancelled.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.690
Stop joking around.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:34.440
Th-Th-This is Old Man Crybaby's!

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:37.190
Found in back alley.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:43.950
We thought we just lost contact with him
since he'd passed out drunk again, but...

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:48.540
He'd never just
leave his precious <i>sake</i> behind.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:51.000
What's happened to Old Man Crybaby?

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:53.880
What a pain in the ass!

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:56.260
And all because of an outsider.

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:57.760
What's that supposed to mean?

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:02.390
Old Man Crybaby must have been
jumped by the Western <i>yokai</i>.

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:03.760
Rat Man!

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:06.180
Considering we're protecting Agnes,

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:09.770
I figured something like this
would happen eventually.

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:10.940
That's enough!

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:13.440
Wh-Wh-What?

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:17.820
A landlord is like a parent
and a tenant is like a child.

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:21.110
Take up your issues about Agnes with me!

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:25.830
I-I was just thinking about
the safety of this country and--

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:27.370
Stop lying!

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:32.290
You're just taking out your anger at
the getaway being cancelled on Agnes.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:37.710
Your right to participate was rescinded,
so you never had a bus seat anyway.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:49.020
Dammit!

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:53.810
Um...

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:57.650
Don't worry about what that loser says.

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:04.110
Okay, let's split up
and find Old Man Crybaby.

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:06.330
I-I'll help, too.

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:07.740
Thanks.

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:10.950
Are those...?

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:16.210
Let's all have some since you made them.

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:17.380
Can we?

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:19.840
Sure.

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:29.180
Those bastards.
Always playing favorites with Agnes.

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:32.230
Who's more important, me or that witch?

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:34.980
Try to cheer up.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.810
Huh? I can have this?

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:40.860
That really gets me right here!

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:43.200
W-Well, if you say so.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:52.660
Man, I don't know who you... are...

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:54.040
but...

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:56.460
You're welcome.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:03.010
<i>SOKAI</i> LIVELY APARTMENT

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:08.350
Hey, hey, hey, hey! The sun's up already!

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:12.520
Hurry down to eat or I'll kiss you!

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:18.480
Cut me some slack.

00:09:18.610 --> 00:09:23.900
I was looking for Old Man Crybaby
from the sky until late last night.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.830
Sand Witch...?

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:55.600
It feels like someone's watchin' me.

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:09.450
I see. Thank you.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:14.450
Where could Old Man Crybaby have gone to?

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:17.660
Old Man Crybaby?

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:21.210
Wait!

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:45.480
UNDER CONSTRUCTION
NO TRESPASSING

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:58.250
Old Man Crybaby?

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:13.010
Who's there?! Coward. Show yourself!

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:15.140
I'm right here.

00:11:25.270 --> 00:11:27.650
You're Backbeard?!

00:11:40.830 --> 00:11:41.920
Rollo Cloth?!

00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:45.420
Hey!

00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:56.930
Old Man Crybaby, Sand Witch, Wally Wall?!

00:11:57.310 --> 00:11:58.770
What's going on?

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:18.330
<i>Hey, Kitaro!</i>

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:21.580
Rat Man, you're all right.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:25.880
We here,

00:12:26.210 --> 00:12:28.460
PROTECT JAPANESE <i>YOKAI</i> RIGHTS!

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:30.840
for the safety and survival
of Japanese <i>yokai</i>,

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:30.840
KICK OUT WESTERN <i>YOKAI</i>

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:36.600
demand that the Western witch, Agnes,
be immediately banished from this country!

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:38.930
GET OUT OF JAPAN, AGNES

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:39.850
Get out of Japan, Western <i>yokai</i>!

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:41.310
AGNES IS A DISEASE!!

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:41.310
Get out!

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:43.100
Get out!

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:44.560
Get out!!

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:48.070
Get out!

00:12:48.190 --> 00:12:49.780
-Get out!
-What's the meaning of this?!

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:54.240
Old Man Crybaby, Sand Witch,
Rollo Cloth, Wally Wall,

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:57.780
and now even Catchick have disappeared!

00:12:58.450 --> 00:13:01.040
Battle-hardened veterans, one by one!

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:04.830
Only the Western <i>yokai</i> could do
something like this!

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:09.670
If we drive out Agnes,
they probably won't attack us anymore.

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:13.510
They might even
return Catchick and the others.

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:19.810
Kitaro, I've got one question for you...

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:22.640
Us or Agnes,

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:25.600
who is more important to you?!

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:27.900
That's not the issue!

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:29.310
Yes it is the issue!

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:37.820
I'm warning you, these aren't
the only guys who agree with me.

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:49.670
You too?

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:55.380
We feel bad for Agnes.

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:59.390
But, Sand Witch is like a mother to us.

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:02.220
If we have to choose one or the other...

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:07.940
Agnes!

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:17.070
HEY! KITARO

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:21.580
KASA-BAKE

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:20.570
-<i>"I sense </i>yokai<i> activity."</i>
-<i>"Scratch, scratch."</i>

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:21.580
<i>"What is this guy...?"</i>

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:27.120
Where could she have gone?

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:34.840
Us or Agnes,
who is more important to you?!

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:39.470
I can't make a choice like that.

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:41.300
Kitaro.

00:14:42.550 --> 00:14:47.680
In times of doubt, you should
listen to the voice in your heart.

00:14:47.810 --> 00:14:51.100
The answer must be there.

00:14:52.610 --> 00:14:54.820
The voice in my heart...

00:14:56.150 --> 00:14:57.440
It's fine.

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:00.200
I can do it alone.

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:05.990
That worked out great.

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:07.910
Keep your promise, okay?

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:09.000
Promise?

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:16.260
You said you'd release Old Man Crybaby
and the others and never attack us again.

00:15:16.710 --> 00:15:21.590
Sorry, but Backbeard-sama
never negotiates.

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:25.720
All we offer anyone
who resists us even once

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:27.720
is despair!

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:37.440
Th-This is...?

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:40.650
Backbeard!

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:42.200
How sad.

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:46.990
To think, you won't call me
Backbeard-sama anymore.

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:48.870
Why would I ever?!

00:15:50.410 --> 00:15:53.130
I sense your despair.

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:55.880
But it's not enough.

00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:00.380
And so,

00:16:03.010 --> 00:16:08.720
I shall show you
the Japanese <i>yokai</i> killing each other.

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:11.600
Now despair!

00:16:14.730 --> 00:16:16.650
This intense <i>yokai</i> activity...

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:17.770
Backbeard?!

00:16:19.110 --> 00:16:22.400
The enemy boss himself has appeared.

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:37.460
Agnes!

00:16:39.050 --> 00:16:42.970
In the name of Backbeard-sama.

00:16:43.090 --> 00:16:45.260
Everyone, what's wrong?!

00:16:45.390 --> 00:16:46.720
Kitaro!

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:51.100
They've all been brainwashed by Backbeard!

00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:53.440
Rat Man!

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:03.070
At this rate...!

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:05.820
Go for the one controlling everyone!

00:17:05.950 --> 00:17:07.030
Right!

00:17:09.030 --> 00:17:10.540
Hair Needles!

00:17:10.660 --> 00:17:11.790
Wally Wall!

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:13.040
It's no good!

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:16.380
Stop it!

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:18.670
Snap out of it, Catchick!

00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:36.190
Kitaro!

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:39.020
I'm fine, Dad.

00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:46.240
Agnes, you belong to me.

00:17:46.990 --> 00:17:52.740
You were born a witch, meaning that
your only place is with me.

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:58.750
That is your destiny.
You cannot escape your destiny.

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:08.010
Now, Kitaro, make your choice.

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:11.260
Kill your friends and survive,

00:18:11.390 --> 00:18:14.520
or die right there.

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:21.020
The voice in my heart says to me,

00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:23.780
"Don't chose either option."

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:25.150
What?

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:27.950
I don't intend to die here.

00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:31.160
But I'll save all of my friends.

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:33.330
Catchick! Wally Wall!

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:36.160
Sand Witch! Old Man Crybaby!

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:39.120
Rollo Cloth! Rat Man!

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:44.250
Agnes, you too!

00:18:51.550 --> 00:18:54.680
Of all the things to say!

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:58.310
The voice in his heart. How heroic!

00:18:58.440 --> 00:18:59.690
Why you...!

00:18:59.810 --> 00:19:01.810
Oh, are you upset?

00:19:02.230 --> 00:19:06.280
I'll show you my one and only
super attack!

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:13.280
Wh-...?!

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:24.750
P-Pee-ew!

00:19:37.220 --> 00:19:39.140
Amazing, Rat Man!

00:19:39.270 --> 00:19:42.560
See what I can do when I get serious.

00:19:44.190 --> 00:19:47.400
Kitaro! Blast up to him!

00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:53.200
Kitaro, go!

00:19:57.620 --> 00:19:58.830
What?!

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:02.330
Agnes!

00:20:02.460 --> 00:20:04.500
Curse you, Kitaro!

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:06.750
<i>I have a place!</i>

00:20:07.340 --> 00:20:09.380
<i>Destiny can be changed!</i>

00:20:23.230 --> 00:20:27.070
<i>Dainaga mi torchi!</i>

00:20:42.210 --> 00:20:44.210
Well done, Agnes.

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:50.550
If your magic is that powerful, you can
become a good core for the Brigadoon.

00:20:57.550 --> 00:21:00.310
Become a core for the Brigadoon?

00:21:01.140 --> 00:21:02.600
What did he mean?

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:19.870
Hmph. Thanks to doing that,
my best clothes are ruined.

00:21:19.990 --> 00:21:23.830
Hey, where is this? Where?

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:27.130
-Where am I? Am I Rollo Cloth?
-I guess I'll get Kitaro to pay for it.

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:28.290
Hey...

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:31.170
Honestly, where have you been?

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:32.840
I don't remember.

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:34.800
Me hungry.

00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:37.220
Hey, do you smell something?

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:39.050
Sniff, sniff... Ugh.

00:21:43.430 --> 00:21:45.440
Answer me this...

00:21:46.690 --> 00:21:49.230
Why did you say I was your friend?

00:21:51.480 --> 00:21:53.070
I don't have a reason.

00:21:56.490 --> 00:21:57.820
Thank you.

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:01.910
And, goodbye...

00:22:03.330 --> 00:22:04.540
Kitaro...

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:10.500
<i>You can't see them
But they're there</i>

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:10.500
<i>mien keredomo orundayo</i>

00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:14.340
<i>"Hello" in the mountains</i>

00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:14.340
<i>yama de yahho</i>

00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:17.260
<i>If you call</i>

00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:17.260
<i>hitokoe yobeba</i>

00:22:17.380 --> 00:22:19.550
<i>An identical "Hello"</i>

00:22:17.380 --> 00:22:19.550
<i>onaji yahho</i>

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:24.850
<i>The Yobuko calls back</i>

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:24.850
<i>yobuko ga kaesu</i>

00:22:25.180 --> 00:22:27.440
<i>A tree spirit living in the mountains</i>

00:22:25.180 --> 00:22:27.440
<i>yama ni sunderu ki no seirei</i>

00:22:30.650 --> 00:22:32.860
<i>A used rag</i>

00:22:30.650 --> 00:22:32.860
<i>tsukatta zoukin</i>

00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:35.740
